# From Apache DataFusion's sqllogictest files (https://github.com/apache/datafusion):
# datafusion/sqllogictest/test_files/negative_zero.slt at commit
# 934691e9af8f11bf4b629f21bb17795abfb84d93, as it is there but for this header
# and the condition lines added before records, under the Apache License 2.0
# (LICENSE beside this file; NOTICE says whose they are).
# transformer: an unconstrained DECIMAL is DECIMAL(38,10)
#
# 28 records: 4 run as DataFusion answers them; 17 skipped by a rule of the
# ledger in docs/gotchas.md (refused-subquery 10, refused-except-intersect 7);
# 7 held for DataFusion, `onlyif datafusion # needs ...`, by what they need: a
# statement the runner does not carry out 2, what a held statement makes 2, a
# clause or construct the engine refuses 1, a function the engine has not 1, a
# type the engine has not 1.

